{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-11 conflict on routing. This spec follows ASM-1: paths are mapped as written (/me), UsePathBase(\"/api\") lets /api/me answer too, and the generated document declares server /api. Mapping under an /api route group (ASM-11) would put /api/me into the document's paths and break conformance with the contract.","ASM-3 ('system starts empty') is overridden by Q-5 and Q-8: the schema is created and a few sample rows are seeded at startup, but only when the database is empty.","Other members exist only as booked and waitlist counts on the session (Q-4). The returned bookedCount and waitlistCount include the demo member. The demo member's waitlist position is stored on their booking row; promotion notices are stored as promoted-at and notice-acknowledged fields on the booking (Q-7).","Precedence of createBooking checks: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started → outside_booking_window → already_booked → class_full → overlap → limit_reached. joinWaitlist: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started → outside_booking_window → already_booked → not_full. The contract lists the codes but gives no order.","Window boundaries are inclusive for allowed actions: a class can be booked when it starts at most 7 days and at least 15 minutes from now. Cancelling is late when the class starts less than 2 hours from now. Undo is allowed when now − createdAt ≤ 5 seconds. A class has started when now ≥ startsAt.","The overlap check uses half-open intervals [startsAt, endsAt): back-to-back classes do not overlap. Only Booked records for sessions that are not studio-cancelled and have not ended count toward overlap; only Booked records for classes not yet started count toward the limit of 10. Waitlist joins are not checked for overlap or the limit.","The contract's examples disagree on availabilityLabel ('2 spots left' vs 'Only 2 left'). This spec uses: 1 → '1 spot left', 2–3 → 'Only N left', ≥4 → 'N spots left'. A full class always uses the 'Full · N on waitlist' form, so a full class with nobody waiting reads 'Full · 0 on waitlist' (REQ-9). The contract gives no example of this case.","A studio-cancelled session always shows actionState disabled with reason 'Cancelled by studio', even when the demo member holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for it (REQ-10, REQ-11). This matches the record being reported as 'Cancelled by studio' in My Bookings.","When the simulate hook runs and the demo member is Waitlisted but not first, SimulationResult.booking is their Waitlisted booking with the new position (REQ-30). booking is null only when the demo member holds no Waitlisted record on that session (REQ-28).","Promotion ignores the overlap and limit rules (ASM-5, ASM-15), so skipReason is always null in this release.","A Booked or Waitlisted record on a studio-cancelled session is reported with status and badge 'Cancelled by studio' and appears in the Past list. Booked/Waitlisted records for classes that have started but not ended stay in Upcoming with canChange false. Waitlisted records whose class has ended appear in neither list. All Cancelled records appear in Past, whatever their class time.","Duplicate-booking protection is the already_booked check inside the same request or transaction. No unique index or locking is added (ASM-8, ASM-16).","Build-time OpenAPI generation is detected when the app runs under the GetDocument.Insider tool, so startup database work can be skipped.","All times in messages are 24-hour Europe/London; the cancel confirmation uses \"today HH:mm\" when the class is on the current London day and \"ddd HH:mm\" otherwise. startsAt/endsAt are serialised as UTC ISO-8601.","DaySummary.hasSessions ignores the type/intensity/timeOfDay filters.","currentStreakWeeks counts back from the current London week; if the current week has no Attended record yet, counting starts from the previous week instead of returning 0.","Rule tests run against a temporary SQLite file through WebApplicationFactory with a fake TimeProvider injected (ASM-9, ASM-14); tests may insert session and booking rows directly to set up a state."],"critic":[{"finding":"REQ-26 says the waitlist checks run \"after not_found and already_booked rules as listed in the assumptions\", but the assumptions' joinWaitlist order puts already_booked after outside_booking_window, so the two give different codes for an already-waitlisted record on a closed-window session.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-34's EARS puts every Booked/Waitlisted record whose class has not ended into upcoming, but AC-34.4 expects a Booked record on a studio-cancelled session tomorrow to appear in past, and the stored row has no 'Cancelled by studio' status to tell them apart.","reqId":"REQ-34","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Stats upcoming (REQ-36) and the limit of 10 (REQ-21 and the assumptions) count Booked records for any session not yet started, so bookings on studio-cancelled sessions still count and use up limit slots, while My Bookings shows them as past and canChange false means the member can't free the slot by cancelling.","reqId":"REQ-36","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The simulate hook doesn't say what happens for studio-cancelled or already-started sessions, or when bookedCount is 0 (the count would go negative). It also lowers bookedCount even when the only booked member is the demo member's own Booked row, which leaves the counts and the rows out of step.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The spec never says whether the stored session counts are other-members-only (as Q-4 suggests) or totals that include the demo member, yet REQ-24, REQ-27 and REQ-28 describe changes to the returned totals and AC-41.3 reads 'booked count equal to capacity' straight from the table, so how the counts are stored and updated is ambiguous.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-37.1 starts the app with an App connection string that can't be opened, but REQ-39 runs EnsureCreated and the seed at startup, which would fail before any request is served; the spec doesn't define what happens when startup schema creation or seeding fails.","reqId":"REQ-37","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-37 (500 storage_failure), REQ-15 (400) and REQ-14 (404 on undo, cancel, leave-waitlist and simulate) assume the contract declares those statuses for every operation, with no contract anchor, while AC-1.2 and AC-2.2 require only declared status codes.","reqId":"REQ-37","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-42 (3–12 sessions, AC-42.1) and REQ-43 (at most 15 / 1–15, AC-43.1) set different seed-size bounds for the same behaviour, and REQ-41's required mix of sessions needs at least 4 sessions, so REQ-42's lower bound of 3 isn't enough.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-2 (p95 ≤ 200 ms, with a leftover '(d2: 50)' draft note) and NFR-3 (p95 ≤ 300 ms) set conflicting latency targets for the same GET /api/schedule measurement.","reqId":"NFR-2","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-7 gives the 'Full · N on waitlist' label only when N > 0 and has no branch for 0 spots with nobody waiting, while REQ-9 separately requires 'Full · 0 on waitlist'; the two label rules overlap and don't match.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-10 doesn't define actionState for a session whose class has ended when the demo member holds a Booked record (reported as Attended) or a Waitlisted record (which, per the assumptions, appears in neither list).","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Undo checks only that the record is Booked and within 5 seconds of createdAt, so a waitlist record that was promoted within 5 seconds could be deleted by undo with no change to the waitlist counts, which breaks 'as if never made'.","reqId":"REQ-22","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-1 requires every non-2xx body to be a contract Error, but no requirement covers non-integer path ids (e.g. /bookings/abc/undo) or framework-level 404/405 responses, which return empty bodies by default.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"'No tables or no data' is not defined against specific tables, so a database with tables but partial data (e.g. bookings but no sessions) gets no defined seed decision, and EnsureCreated does nothing on a database that already has a different schema.","reqId":"REQ-39","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-40 relies on detecting the GetDocument.Insider tool to skip database work during the build, but this is stated only in an assumption, with no anchor in the csproj or Program.cs.","reqId":"REQ-40","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The demo member's identity values (id 1, 'Alex Rivera', 'AR', 'Unlimited Monthly') and the exact message strings across REQ-16 to REQ-32 have no anchor to the contract or the request.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-41.3, AC-16.4, AC-28.1 (promoted-at) and AC-33.1 (notice-acknowledged) check internal table columns rather than a public API surface.","reqId":"AC-41.3","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-4 adds a write-latency budget (p95 < 300 ms) that the intent never asked for.","reqId":"NFR-4","rubric":4,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 41 requirements, about 4 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","passed":false},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 of all 4xx/5xx responses produced by the acceptance and rule tests contain an exception type name, the text \"Exception\", a line starting with \"   at \" or SQL text; 100% have a code from the 13-value enum","text":"Error responses never expose raw server errors: every non-2xx response body is a contract Error with a code from the enum and a plain message."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 latency of GET /api/schedule ≤ 200 ms over 100 sequential calls (d2: 50) against the seeded SQLite database on a developer/test machine","text":"GET /schedule on the seeded database answers quickly (stricter reading from d2/d3)."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"p95 latency ≤ 300 ms over 100 sequential GET /api/schedule calls against the seeded SQLite file on a developer machine","text":"GET /schedule on the seeded database answers quickly enough for the web app's 1-second render target (d1 reading)."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"p95 latency under 300 ms over 100 sequential write requests on the seeded database","text":"Write operations (book, waitlist, cancel, leave, undo) respond within the budget that lets the web app reconcile its optimistic update."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"20 sequential identical POST /api/bookings calls for one session leave exactly 1 non-cancelled booking row; 1 response is 201 and 19 are 409 already_booked","text":"Repeated Book taps do not create duplicate bookings."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"0 differences reported by the factory's comparison of App.Api/openapi/built.json against contracts/openapi.yaml on every build","text":"The generated OpenAPI document stays identical to the locked contract."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"≥ 8 rule tests, one per §10 bullet, with a 100% pass rate in dotnet test","text":"App.Tests contains automated business-rule tests run through WebApplicationFactory with a fake TimeProvider, covering the §10 list: booking with spots, full plus waitlist join, promotion on cancel, booking window, late-cancel flag, overlap, 10-booking limit, and past/studio-cancelled rejection."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"The App.Tests rule suite passes 10 out of 10 consecutive runs with a fake clock","text":"Business-rule tests are deterministic because time comes from an injected TimeProvider."}],"outOfScope":["Web screens, design system, dark mode, motion, responsive layout and accessibility work; the web app is built in its own repo (request)","The end-to-end UI test (schedule → filter → book → My Bookings → cancel), which belongs to the web repo (ASM-9)","Seeding 40+ sessions over two weeks with 5 instructors as described in §4.3; only a few rows are seeded (Q-8)","Editing contracts/openapi.yaml, including its description that mentions local storage (ASM-10)","Sign-in, sign-up, authentication and multiple members","Payments, credits, class packs, membership purchase and membership management","Email, SMS and push notifications; promotion is announced only through the promotion-notices endpoints","Staff, instructor or admin screens/endpoints and schedule editing","Calendar export, multiple locations, native apps and multi-language support (§12)","Making rule numbers (7 days, 15 minutes, 2 hours, 5 seconds, limit 10) or the demo member configurable; they stay code constants (ASM-6, ASM-13)","Changing the existing GET / \"API is up\" route, which stays as it is and stays out of the OpenAPI document (ASM-2, ASM-12)","Storing other members as individual records; they exist only as counts on the session (Q-4)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A clean checkout","id":"AC-1.1","level":"job","then":"The file App.Api/openapi/built.json exists, lists exactly the 13 operationIds of the contract under the same path and method, and its servers list has url /api","when":"dotnet build runs on App.Api"},{"given":"The solution has been built, which writes App.Api/openapi/built.json","id":"AC-1.2","level":"job","then":"The returned count of differences is 0 for paths, methods, operationIds, parameters, request bodies, response status codes, schemas (required fields, property types, nullability, enum values) and the server url /api","when":"The factory's contract comparison job compares the built document with contracts/openapi.yaml"},{"given":"The generated file App.Api/openapi/built.json","id":"AC-1.3","level":"job","then":"The list has no entry for \"/\" and contains exactly getMember, getSchedule, getSession, createBooking, undoBooking, cancelBooking, joinWaitlist, leaveWaitlist, getMyBookings, getStats, listPromotionNotices, acknowledgePromotionNotices and simulateOtherMemberCancellation","when":"A test reads its paths list"},{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body is \"API is up\"","when":"A client sends GET /"},{"given":"The build has run","id":"AC-1.5","level":"job","then":"The file content is unchanged","when":"contracts/openapi.yaml is compared with its committed version"}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":8,"lineStart":6,"path":"App.Api/App.Api.csproj","quote":"    <!-- the build writes the API's OpenAPI document here; the factory compares it with contracts/openapi.yaml -->\n    <OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/openapi</OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>\n    <OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>--file-name built</OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>"}],"ears":"When the build generates the API's OpenAPI document into App.Api/openapi (file built.json), the API shall emit a document with the same 13 operationIds, paths (as written in the contract, without the /api prefix), HTTP methods, parameters, request bodies, response status codes and component schemas as contracts/openapi.yaml, with server url /api and without the existing GET / route (which keeps answering \"API is up\"), leaving contracts/openapi.yaml unedited.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-12"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running on seeded data","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses have status 200 and identical JSON bodies","when":"GET /me and GET /api/me are called"},{"given":"The API is running on seeded data","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"Every response status is one the contract declares for that operation, and no call returns 404 for an unmapped route or 405","when":"Each of the 13 contract operations is called once under /api with a valid request"},{"given":"The API is running with the seeded database","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"Every response status is 200 and every response body is JSON that matches the contract schema for that operation","when":"A client sends GET /api/me, GET /api/schedule, GET /api/me/bookings, GET /api/me/stats and GET /api/me/promotion-notices"}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":13,"lineStart":9,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"var app = builder.Build();\napp.UseCors();\napp.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n\napp.Run();"}],"ears":"The API shall answer each of the 13 operations of contracts/openapi.yaml with the HTTP method the contract declares, both at the /api-prefixed path (for example GET /api/me) and at the path as written (for example GET /me).","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the body fields are id=1, name=\"Alex Rivera\", initials=\"AR\", membership=\"Unlimited Monthly\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/me"}],"ears":"When GET /me is called, the API shall return status 200 with the demo member id 1, name \"Alex Rivera\", initials \"AR\" and membership \"Unlimited Monthly\".","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-6","ASM-13"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T08:00:00Z and sessions exist on Mon 12 and Wed 14 Oct only","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response has today \"2026-10-14\", date \"2026-10-14\", weekStart \"2026-10-12\", canGoPreviousWeek false, canGoNextWeek true, 7 days whose third entry is {date \"2026-10-14\", label \"Wed 14\", isToday true, hasSessions true} and whose Tue 13 entry has hasSessions false","when":"GET /schedule is called with no date"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14 10:00 Europe/London, sessions exist on 2026-10-14 at 18:00, 07:00 and 12:30 London (one of them Cancelled by studio) and no session exists on 2026-10-18","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200; the days list has 7 entries from \"Mon 12\" to \"Sun 18\" with isToday true only for 2026-10-14 and hasSessions false for 2026-10-18; the sessions list has 3 entries in the order 07:00, 12:30, 18:00 including the studio-cancelled one","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule with no query"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T08:00:00Z","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 with weekStart \"2026-10-19\", canGoPreviousWeek true, canGoNextWeek false and no day with isToday true","when":"GET /schedule?date=2026-10-21 is called"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T23:30:00Z (00:30 on 15 Oct in Europe/London)","id":"AC-4.4","level":"api","then":"The response field today is \"2026-10-15\"","when":"GET /schedule is called with no date"}],"ears":"When GET /schedule is called with a valid or absent date, the API shall return status 200 with today (the Europe/London date), date (the parameter, or today when absent), weekStart (the Monday of that date's week), canGoPreviousWeek true only when date is in next week, canGoNextWeek true only when date is in the current week, 7 days Monday to Sunday each labelled \"ddd d\" with isToday and hasSessions (true when at least one session starts that day, ignoring filters), and the selected day's sessions, including studio-cancelled ones, ordered by startsAt ascending.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7","ASM-14"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T08:00:00Z","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 400 and each body field code is \"invalid_request\" with a non-empty message","when":"GET /api/schedule is called with date=2026-10-11, then date=2026-10-26, then date=2026-10-05, then date=not-a-date, then type=Zumba"}],"ears":"If GET /schedule is called with a date that is malformed or outside the current and next Europe/London week, or with a type, intensity or timeOfDay value not in the contract enums, then the API shall return status 400 with Error code invalid_request.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"On 2026-10-15 there are sessions Yoga/Low at 11:59, Yoga/Medium at 12:00, Spin/High at 16:59, HIIT/High at 17:00 (Europe/London) and a studio-cancelled Yoga/Low at 18:00","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions list is exactly [Yoga 12:00, HIIT 17:00, cancelled Yoga 18:00] in that order","when":"GET /schedule?date=2026-10-15&type=Yoga&type=HIIT&timeOfDay=Afternoon&timeOfDay=Evening is called"},{"given":"The same sessions","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions list contains only the Yoga/Low 11:59 session","when":"GET /schedule?date=2026-10-15&intensity=Low&timeOfDay=Morning is called"},{"given":"On 2026-10-14 there are a Yoga Low session at 07:00 London, a Pilates Medium session at 12:00 London, and a Boxing Medium session at 17:00 London","id":"AC-6.3","level":"api","then":"The returned sessions lists are [Yoga, Boxing], [Pilates 12:00] and [Boxing 17:00] respectively","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?date=2026-10-14&type=Yoga&type=Boxing, then ?date=2026-10-14&timeOfDay=Afternoon, then ?date=2026-10-14&timeOfDay=Evening&intensity=Medium"},{"given":"On the selected day there are a Yoga Low session at 07:00, a Yoga High session at 12:00, a Spin Low session at 17:00 and a Boxing Medium session at 16:59 (London)","id":"AC-6.4","level":"api","then":"The first response sessions list contains exactly the 07:00 Yoga and 17:00 Spin sessions, and the second exactly the 12:00 and 16:59 sessions","when":"A client sends GET /api/schedule?type=Yoga&type=Spin&intensity=Low, then ?timeOfDay=Afternoon"}],"ears":"When GET /schedule includes type, intensity or timeOfDay values, the API shall return in sessions only the selected day's sessions (including studio-cancelled ones) that match at least one listed value of every supplied filter, ignoring filters that are not supplied, where Morning is a Europe/London start before 12:00, Afternoon is 12:00 to 16:59 and Evening is 17:00 or later.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","ASM-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Scheduled sessions with capacity/booked/waitlist of 20/14/0, 12/10/0, 12/11/0, 16/16/3 and a studio-cancelled session 20/0/0","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"The availabilityLabel values are \"6 spots left\", \"Only 2 left\", \"1 spot left\", \"Full · 3 on waitlist\" and \"Cancelled\", and the capacityLabel values are \"6 of 20 spots left\", \"2 of 12 spots left\", \"1 of 12 spots left\", \"0 of 16 spots left\" and \"20 of 20 spots left\"","when":"GET /sessions/{id} is called for each"},{"given":"A Scheduled session has capacity 16, 16 booked by other members and 3 others on the waitlist","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response fields are bookedCount=16 and waitlistCount=3","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"},{"given":"A session has status Cancelled by studio","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"The response fields are status=\"Cancelled by studio\" and availabilityLabel=\"Cancelled\"","when":"A client sends GET /api/sessions/{id}"}],"ears":"The API shall return in every Session bookedCount and waitlistCount that include both the demo member and the other members, capacityLabel \"{spotsLeft} of {capacity} spots left\", and availabilityLabel \"Cancelled\" for a studio-cancelled session, otherwise \"Full · N on waitlist\" when full with N > 0 waiting, \"1 spot left\" for 1 spot, \"Only N left\" for 2 or 3 spots, and \"N spots left\" for 4 or more spots.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Scheduled session has capacity 16, bookedCount 16 and waitlistCount 0","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response field availabilityLabel is \"Full · 0 on waitlist\"","when":"GET /sessions/{id} is called"}],"ears":"While a Scheduled session is full, the API shall return its availabilityLabel as \"Full · {waitlistCount} on waitlist\", which gives \"Full · 0 on waitlist\" when nobody is waiting.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-3"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T08:00:00Z and the demo member holds no record for sessions starting at T+1d (8 of 12 booked), T+1d (12 of 12 booked, 2 waiting), T+8d, T+10min and T-5min","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The actionState values returned are {kind book, canChange true, spotsLeft 4}, {kind join_waitlist, position 3}, {kind disabled, canChange false, reason \"Booking opens 7 days before class\"}, {kind disabled, reason \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\"} and {kind disabled, reason \"Class has started\"}, each with myBookingId null","when":"GET /sessions/{id} is called for each"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T08:00:00Z and the demo member has Booked record 501 for a session starting at 09:30Z and Waitlisted record 502 at position 2 for another session starting at 10:00Z","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"The first response has actionState {kind booked, canChange true, bookingId 501, lateCancellation true} with myBookingId 501, and the second has {kind waitlisted, canChange true, bookingId 502, position 2} with myBookingId 502","when":"GET /sessions/{id} is called for both"},{"given":"The clock is 2026-10-14T09:00:00Z, a full session starting tomorrow has 3 others on the waitlist, and a session starting tomorrow has capacity 12 and 10 booked, neither with a demo record","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api"